---
interface Props{kind:string}
const {kind}=Astro.props;
const captions:Record<string,string>={
 'parcel-detour':'Invented three-origin, two-destination network. Direct: six loaded trips, 480 vehicle-km; via hub: five trips, 230 vehicle-km. Each parcel travels 80 km direct or 100 km via the hub. Empty trips, sorting, collection and final delivery are excluded. The Delivery Lab uses a different, four-by-four Euclidean example.',
 'barcode':'Fictional parcel P has two recorded events: dispatched at depot A at 09:10 and received at depot B at 12:10. At 11:00, the earlier record does not establish its current position. The line connects observations; it is not a continuous track.',
 'box-space':'Invented external box: 40 × 30 × 20 cm = 24 L. Product envelope: 20 × 15 × 10 cm = 3 L, or 12.5% of the outside volume. The remainder includes walls, protection and unmeasured gaps. It is not a measured air percentage.',
 'last-mile':'Invented 20-stop round: 19 one-minute driving intervals plus 20 three-minute handovers = 79 minutes. Halving only travel gives 69.5 minutes; halving only handover gives 49 minutes. Approach and return travel are excluded.',
 'container':'Invented 100-carton shipment across three vehicle changes: 100 × 2 × 3 = 600 carton-handling actions, or 1 × 2 × 3 = 6 container-handling actions. These are different units of work, not equivalent durations. Packing, unpacking and intermediate yard moves are excluded.',
 'returns':'Fictional return-centre rules for three lamps. Receipt leads to assessment, then different possible routes according to condition. These are illustrative routing decisions, not observed business practices or electrical-testing instructions.'
};
---
<figure class="article-figure">
<div class="diagram-mobile">
{kind==='parcel-detour'&&<><strong>Farther per parcel. Fewer loaded kilometres.</strong><table><caption>Constructed network · same 60 parcels</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col">Direct</th><th scope="col">Hub</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Loaded trips</th><td>6</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Vehicle-km</th><td>480</td><td>230</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Km per parcel</th><td>80</td><td>100</td></tr></tbody></table></>}
{kind==='barcode'&&<><strong>An identity joins two observations.</strong><div class="diagram-row"><span>09:10<br /><b>Depot A</b></span><span>Dispatched<br />Parcel P</span></div><div class="diagram-row"><span>11:00<br /><b>No new record</b></span><span>Current position<br />not established</span></div><div class="diagram-row"><span>12:10<br /><b>Depot B</b></span><span>Received<br />Parcel P</span></div></>}
{kind==='box-space'&&<><strong>Two bounding boxes. Different questions.</strong><table><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Outer parcel</th><td>24 L</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Product envelope</th><td>3 L</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Envelope fraction</th><td>12.5%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The complement is not measured air.</p></>}
{kind==='last-mile'&&<><strong>What changed on the clock?</strong><table><caption>Constructed 20-stop round, minutes</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Case</th><th scope="col">Travel</th><th scope="col">Handover</th><th scope="col">Total</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Baseline</th><td>19</td><td>60</td><td>79</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Half travel</th><td>9.5</td><td>60</td><td>69.5</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Half handover</th><td>19</td><td>30</td><td>49</td></tr></tbody></table></>}
{kind==='container'&&<><strong>Change the unit being handled.</strong><table><caption>100 cartons · three vehicle changes</caption><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Loose cartons</th><td>600 carton actions</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">One enclosure</th><td>6 container actions</td></tr></tbody></table><p>An action is not a common unit of time.</p></>}
{kind==='returns'&&<><strong>Received is not the final outcome.</strong><div class="diagram-row"><span>Eligible unopened</span><span>Checks → ordinary stock</span></div><div class="diagram-row"><span>Working, cosmetic marks</span><span>Describe → used channel</span></div><div class="diagram-row"><span>Damaged cord</span><span>Hold → appropriate assessment</span></div></>}
</div>
<svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 600 270" role="img" aria-label={captions[kind]}>
{kind==='parcel-detour'&&<><text x="25" y="35" font-size="22">Distance for whom?</text><text x="25" y="92" font-size="18">Direct</text><rect x="160" y="65" width="370" height="35" fill="var(--ink)"/><text x="160" y="126" font-size="18">480 loaded vehicle-km · 80 km per parcel</text><text x="25" y="187" font-size="18">Hub</text><rect x="160" y="160" width="177.29" height="35" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="160" y="221" font-size="18">230 loaded vehicle-km · 100 km per parcel</text></>}
{kind==='barcode'&&<><text x="25" y="35" font-size="22">An identity joins observations.</text><path d="M70 110H520" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 7"/><circle cx="70" cy="110" r="12" fill="var(--ink)"/><circle cx="520" cy="110" r="12" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="70" y="82" font-size="20">09:10</text><text x="520" y="82" text-anchor="end" font-size="20">12:10</text><text x="70" y="153" font-size="18">Depot A · dispatched</text><text x="520" y="153" text-anchor="end" font-size="18">Depot B · received</text><text x="25" y="218" font-size="19">At 11:00: the last record is not a current position.</text><text x="25" y="247" font-size="16" class="diagram-note">FICTIONAL PARCEL P · NO CONTINUOUS TRACK</text></>}
{kind==='box-space'&&<><text x="25" y="35" font-size="22">Compare envelopes. Keep the boundary.</text><text x="25" y="85" font-size="19">Outer box: 40 × 30 × 20 cm = 24 L</text><rect x="25" y="108" width="520" height="38" fill="var(--rule)"/><rect x="25" y="108" width="65" height="38" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="25" y="184" font-size="19">Product envelope: 20 × 15 × 10 cm = 3 L</text><text x="25" y="228" font-size="24" class="diagram-accent">3 ÷ 24 = 12.5%</text><text x="260" y="228" font-size="18">Not an air measurement.</text></>}
{kind==='last-mile'&&<><text x="25" y="35" font-size="22">Travel and handover use different minutes.</text>{[{y:85,t:19,h:60,label:'Baseline',sum:'79'},{y:145,t:9.5,h:60,label:'Half travel',sum:'69.5'},{y:205,t:19,h:30,label:'Half handover',sum:'49'}].map(r=><><text x="25" y={r.y+5} font-size="17">{r.label}</text><rect x="178" y={r.y-17} width={r.t*4} height="26" fill="var(--ink)"/><rect x={178+r.t*4} y={r.y-17} width={r.h*4} height="26" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x={190+(r.t+r.h)*4} y={r.y+4} font-size="19">{r.sum}</text></>)}<text x="178" y="251" font-size="17">Ink: travel · Rust: handover · Minutes</text></>}
{kind==='container'&&<><text x="25" y="35" font-size="22">Change the object that crosses the transfer.</text><text x="60" y="124" font-size="55">600</text><text x="350" y="124" font-size="55" class="diagram-accent">6</text><text x="60" y="165" font-size="20">carton actions</text><text x="350" y="165" font-size="20">container actions</text><path d="M25 192H555" stroke="var(--rule)"/><text x="25" y="234" font-size="19">Different units. No time-saving ratio implied.</text></>}
{kind==='returns'&&<><text x="25" y="35" font-size="22">Receipt opens a decision.</text><text x="300" y="83" text-anchor="middle" font-size="24">Assess condition</text><path d="M300 100v30M100 160v-30h400v30M300 130v30" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>{[{x:100,a:'Unopened',b:'Ordinary stock'},{x:300,a:'Cosmetic marks',b:'Used channel'},{x:500,a:'Damage',b:'Assessment'}].map(p=><><circle cx={p.x} cy="174" r="10" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x={p.x} y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18">{p.a}</text><text x={p.x} y="242" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18">{p.b}</text></>)}</>}
</svg>
<figcaption>{captions[kind]}</figcaption>
</figure>
